"Agglayer" means the protocol to aggregate networks that consists of a unified
bridge providing cryptoasset fungibility, proof aggregation providing gas cost
reductions, and methods for low-latency, secure cross-chain asset and message
transfers, known as the "Agglayer".

"Production Use" means use of the Licensed Work (or any derivative work) in a
production environment that is accessible to end users or third parties and
supports live transactions or real-value activity.

"Permitted Deployment" means a deployment of the Licensed Work that is operated
solely to support one or more blockchain networks that are connected to Agglayer
in a manner approved by Licensor, and that routes or supports bridging and/or
messaging via Agglayer (an "Agglayer-Connected Deployment").

"Bridge-as-a-Service" means offering the Licensed Work to third parties as a
hosted, managed, or multi-tenant service (whether for a fee or otherwise) for
use with third-party chains or customers, other than operating a Permitted
Deployment for an Agglayer-Connected Deployment.

